// This Pine Script™ code is subject to the terms of the Mozilla Public License 2.0 at https://mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/
// =============================================================================
// JDUN | 15m ORB | Combined
//
// ONE indicator: the JDUN trade engine (Jaydon's two webinars, his rules in his
// order) with the GD context layer from USE-15m-ORB-Jinxed merged on top.
//
// WHAT CAME FROM WHERE
//   TRADE ENGINE — JDUN. Opening range, trend-setting candle, golden pocket /
//     two-bar entry, R-multiple targets, two-trade daily cap, R backtest table.
//     Unchanged from JDUN-ORB.pine.
//   CONTEXT LAYER — from the Jinxed script's GD merge: the fast/slow EMA pair,
//     the EMA-cross-on-volume heads-up signals (with their own two alerts), the
//     sweep + reclaim diamonds, and the alert-window background shading.
//     None of these open a position. They have no TP and no SL.
//
// DELIBERATELY NOT CARRIED OVER
//   The fluxchart state-machine engine from the Jinxed script (Sensitivity,
//     Dynamic/ATR take-profits, the retest counter). It is a SECOND trade engine
//     firing on the SAME alert names — Buy / Sell / Take Profit 1-3 / Stop Loss —
//     so running both would send two conflicting orders to the same PickMyTrade
//     webhook. The Jinxed script's own Jay mode already reimplemented the rules
//     that the JDUN engine implements here, so no behaviour is lost.
//   The volume profile. That is the blue box — it is gone, as asked. Every level
//     on this chart is now a line.
//
// LEVEL LINES
//   Every reference level — PM high/low, previous day high/low, Asia high/low,
//   POC, ORB high, ORB mid, ORB low — is drawn as a full line that starts at the
//   open of a PREVIOUS session and runs right to the live candle, with its name
//   and price at the right-hand end. How far back it reaches is the "Extend
//   levels back" input (1 = yesterday's open, the default). The old 3-bar stub
//   is gone.
//
// HIS SEQUENCE
//   1. Before the open, mark the levels: pre-market H/L, previous day H/L,
//      Asia H/L, VWAP, point of control.
//   2. Let the first 15 minutes form the opening range. NO TRADES in that window.
//      "9:30 to 9:45 equals no trades. Let the market show you its hand."
//   3. Wait for a 5-minute candle to CLOSE beyond the range. Never mid-candle.
//   4. That candle must be a TREND-SETTING CANDLE: full body, minimal wick,
//      rising volume. A big candle on weak volume is an "anomaly" — someone is
//      lying — and is skipped.
//   5. Draw a fib across that candle. Enter the pullback into the 0.5-0.618
//      GOLDEN POCKET, ideally where it stacks with one of the marked levels.
//   6. If the move is too aggressive to retrace that far, use the TWO-BAR
//      SETUP instead: a shallower pullback measured across both candles.
//   7. Stop goes beyond the trend-setting candle. Hard stop, never mental.
//   8. Trim ~70% at 1R and move the stop to break-even. Rest at 1.5R and 2R.
//   9. Two trades a day maximum. Two losses and the day is over.
//  10. Trade the first 1-2 hours. Flat before the close.
//
// HIS NUMBERS AS DEFAULTS
//   Targets are R-multiples off the actual stop distance (1R / 1.5R / 2R), not
//   ATR — that is how he sizes every trade he describes.
//   Alert window is 09:30-11:00. Max stop 40 points ("40-50 acceptable, 100 too
//   wide"). Both are inputs.
//
// EXECUTION — WHAT WAITS FOR A CANDLE AND WHAT DOES NOT
//   ARMING waits. A setup only exists once a 5-minute candle has CLOSED beyond the
//     range and passed the quality tests. That is his rule and it is untouched.
//   THE ENTRY does not wait, by default. The Buy/Sell alert fires the instant price
//     trades into the golden pocket, the same way TP and SL already fire on touch.
//     The zone test is built from the bar's running high and low, which only widen
//     as the candle forms, so an early fire cannot repaint — the bar-close answer is
//     identical, the alert just arrives sooner. Turn it off with "Fire entries in
//     real time" to go back to waiting for the close.
//     The one exception is Entry model = Level Retest, which tests the close itself
//     and so cannot be known before the candle ends. It always waits.
//   TP AND SL do not wait, including on the entry bar itself: after a real-time fill
//     the entry bar is measured from the live price, so a target reached seconds
//     later is reported at once rather than on the next candle.
//   SET THE ALERT TO "ONCE PER BAR", not "Once Per Bar Close", or TradingView holds
//     every one of these until the candle finishes and none of the above applies.
//   Alert names match the previous script (Buy / Sell / Take Profit 1-3 / Stop
//   Loss / Close All / Flatten) so existing PickMyTrade webhooks carry over.
// =============================================================================

//@version=6
indicator('JDUN | 15m ORB | Combined', overlay = true,
     max_lines_count = 500, max_labels_count = 500, max_boxes_count = 500,
     max_bars_back = 5000)

// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// INPUTS
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

// ── Session and opening range ──
gS = 'Session & Opening Range'
tzSess    = input.string('America/New_York', 'Timezone for all session times', group = gS, tooltip = 'Every session field in this script is read in this timezone, so the times you type are the times you mean. Handles DST automatically.')
rthSess   = input.session('0930-1600', 'Regular session', group = gS)
pmSess    = input.session('0400-0930', 'Pre-market window', group = gS, tooltip = 'He marks pre-market from 4:00am, not 8:00 — he calls this out explicitly.')
asiaSess  = input.session('1800-0300', 'Asia session', group = gS, tooltip = 'Crosses midnight, which Pine handles. Adjust if your Asia definition differs.')
orbMins   = input.int(15, 'Opening range length (minutes)', minval = 5, maxval = 60, step = 5, group = gS, tooltip = 'The first three 5-minute candles. Nothing can trade until this window closes.')

// ── Entry ──
gE = 'Entry'
entryMode = input.string('Golden Pocket', 'Entry model', options = ['Golden Pocket', 'Level Retest', 'Either'], group = gE, tooltip = 'GOLDEN POCKET: enter the pullback into the 0.5-0.618 fib of the trend-setting candle. His primary method. LEVEL RETEST: the simpler version from his first webinar — enter when price comes back and touches the broken range level itself. EITHER: whichever happens first.')
useTwoBar = input.bool(true, 'Two-bar setup fallback', group = gE, tooltip = 'For aggressive trends that never retrace to 0.5. If a second aggressive candle extends the move, a shallower zone is measured across both candles instead. His words: "the only reason you trade a two bar is in the cases of aggressive trends where you dont retest the 50%."')
twoBarLo  = input.float(0.236, 'Two-bar zone start', minval = 0.1, maxval = 0.5, step = 0.014, group = gE)
twoBarHi  = input.float(0.382, 'Two-bar zone end', minval = 0.2, maxval = 0.6, step = 0.018, group = gE)
rtEntry   = input.bool(true, 'Fire entries in real time (on touch)', group = gE, tooltip = 'ON: the Buy/Sell alert fires the INSTANT price trades into the golden pocket, the same way TP and SL already fire on touch — you are not waiting for the 5-minute candle to finish. This is how the pullback is actually traded: a resting limit order at the zone. OFF: the entry waits for the bar to close, the original behaviour.\n\nTwo things to know. The TradingView alert must be set to "Once Per Bar", not "Once Per Bar Close", or it will still wait for the candle. And this applies to the Golden Pocket and two-bar zones only — see the Entry model tooltip.')
validBars = input.int(15, 'Setup valid for N bars', minval = 3, maxval = 60, group = gE, tooltip = 'How long after the trend-setting candle the entry zone stays live. After this the setup is discarded and the script waits for a fresh break.')
useConflu = input.bool(false, 'Require a stacked key level', group = gE, tooltip = 'His highest-probability condition: the fib zone lining up with a marked level. ON means the entry must also be within the distance below of PM H/L, previous day H/L, Asia H/L, VWAP, POC or the ORB midline. This is a strict filter — expect noticeably fewer trades.')
confluPts = input.float(10.0, 'Stacked level distance (points)', minval = 0.25, step = 0.25, group = gE)

// ── Trend-setting candle quality ──
gQ = 'Trend-Setting Candle'
minBodyPct = input.int(50, 'Minimum body % of range', minval = 10, maxval = 100, group = gQ, tooltip = 'His "full body, no or minimal wick". A wick more than half the candle invalidates it.')
needVolUp  = input.bool(true, 'Require rising volume', group = gQ, tooltip = 'Volume above its average AND higher than the previous bar. His auction analogy: rising volume means buyers are bidding aggressively, not that there are simply more of them.')
volLen     = input.int(20, 'Volume average length', minval = 5, group = gQ)
useAnomaly = input.bool(true, 'Reject anomalies', group = gQ, tooltip = 'His "anomaly": a large candle on BELOW-average volume. Size and participation disagree, so the move is a trap.')
anomalyMlt = input.float(1.5, 'Anomaly size (x ATR)', minval = 0.5, step = 0.25, group = gQ)

// ── Risk and targets ──
gR = 'Risk & Targets'
tp1R       = input.float(1.0, 'TP1 (R)', minval = 0.25, step = 0.25, group = gR, tooltip = 'He trims 60-75% here and moves the stop to break-even.')
tp2R       = input.float(1.5, 'TP2 (R)', minval = 0.5, step = 0.25, group = gR)
tp3R       = input.float(2.0, 'TP3 (R) — runner', minval = 0.5, step = 0.25, group = gR)
trimPct    = input.float(0.7, 'Trim fraction at TP1', minval = 0.1, maxval = 0.95, step = 0.05, group = gR, tooltip = 'Used by the backtest table to weight realised R. He states 60-75%.')
tp2HodLod  = input.bool(false, 'TP2 = high/low of day instead', group = gR, tooltip = 'His stated primary target is a new high or low of day. Falls back to the R multiple if that is closer than 1R away.')
beAfterTP1 = input.bool(true, 'Stop to break-even after TP1', group = gR, tooltip = 'Non-negotiable for him: never let a winner turn into a loser.')
stopPad    = input.int(2, 'Stop padding (ticks)', minval = 0, maxval = 20, group = gR, tooltip = 'How far beyond the trend-setting candle the stop sits.')
maxStopPts = input.float(40.0, 'Max stop distance (points, 0 = off)', minval = 0, step = 5, group = gR, tooltip = 'Reject the setup if the stop is wider than this. His guidance: 20-30 points on NQ is ideal, 40-50 acceptable, 100 far too wide. Set 0 to disable.')

// ── Daily limits ──
gD = 'Daily Limits'
maxTrades  = input.int(2, 'Max trades per day', minval = 1, maxval = 10, group = gD, tooltip = '"You are a day trader, not a trade-every-day trader. One good trade a day, two max."')
maxLosses  = input.int(2, 'Max losses per day', minval = 1, maxval = 10, group = gD, tooltip = 'His circuit breaker: "Two full-size losses and I am done. I do not care if the next setup is the best one of the year."')

// ── Alerts ──
gA = 'Alerts'
alertWindow  = input.session('0930-1100', 'Alert window', group = gA, tooltip = 'He trades the first 1-2 hours and cites his own win-rate data for it. Read in the timezone set at the top.')
bufTicks     = input.int(1, 'TP/SL buffer (ticks)', minval = 0, maxval = 20, group = gA, tooltip = 'Fires the exit alert this many ticks early so the market order fills near the intended price.')
showWindowBg = input.bool(false, 'Shade the alert window on the chart', group = gA, tooltip = 'Tints the background while the alert window is open, so you can see at a glance when the engine is allowed to fire.')
lockTF       = input.bool(true, 'Lock alerts to signal timeframe', group = gA, tooltip = 'A TradingView alert permanently captures the chart timeframe it was created on. This stops one made on the wrong chart from ever firing.')
signalTF     = input.string('5', 'Signal timeframe (minutes)', options = ['1', '2', '3', '5', '10', '15'], group = gA, tooltip = 'He executes on the 5-minute and refuses to go lower.')
flatSess     = input.session('0930-1530', 'Flatten after', group = gA, tooltip = 'Any position still open when this window ends gets the Close All alert. End time = your hard flat-by deadline.')

// ── Levels ──
gL = 'Levels'
showPM    = input.bool(true, 'Pre-market high / low', group = gL)
showPrevD = input.bool(true, 'Previous day high / low', group = gL)
showAsia  = input.bool(true, 'Asia high / low', group = gL)
showVWAP  = input.bool(true, 'VWAP', group = gL)
showPOC   = input.bool(true, 'Point of control', group = gL)
pocTicks  = input.int(4, 'POC bucket size (ticks)', minval = 1, maxval = 100, group = gL)
showMid   = input.bool(true, 'ORB midline', group = gL, tooltip = 'The 50% of the opening range. He calls it "the hidden gem" and says to respect it.')
extendDays = input.int(1, 'Extend levels back (sessions)', minval = 0, maxval = 10, group = gL, tooltip = 'How far LEFT every level line reaches. 1 = the line starts at yesterday\'s session open and runs to the live candle, so you can see whether yesterday respected it. 0 = start at today\'s open. The label always sits at the right-hand end, beside the forming candle.')
showLbls  = input.bool(true, 'Label every level', group = gL)

// ── Visuals ──
gV = 'Visuals'
showORB   = input.bool(true, 'Opening range lines', group = gV)
orbHiCol  = input.color(color.green, 'ORB high', inline = 'orb', group = gV)
orbLoCol  = input.color(color.red, 'ORB low', inline = 'orb', group = gV)
showZone  = input.bool(true, 'Entry zone while live', group = gV, tooltip = 'The two YELLOW lines: the 0.5 and 0.618 fib of the trend-setting candle — the golden pocket. Drawn while a setup is armed, gone once it triggers or expires. A two-bar setup uses the same pair of lines at its shallower levels.')
showTradeLines = input.bool(true, 'Entry / SL / TP lines on every trade', group = gV, tooltip = 'Draws Entry, SL, TP1, TP2 and TP3 as horizontal lines from the entry bar to the end of that trading day, for past trades as well as the live one — so you can see every target including the ones price never reached.')
showTradeLbls  = input.bool(true, 'Label the live trade levels', group = gV, tooltip = 'Prints TP1/TP2/TP3/SL with their prices at the right-hand edge while a trade is open.')
showDash  = input.bool(true, 'Dashboard', group = gV)
showBT    = input.bool(true, 'Backtest table', group = gV)
dashPos   = input.string('Top Right', 'Dashboard position', options = ['Top Right', 'Right Center', 'Top Center'], group = gV)
btPos     = input.string('Top Center', 'Backtest position', options = ['Top Right', 'Right Center', 'Top Center'], group = gV)

// ── EMA cross + volume  [from the GD layer] ──
// A standalone momentum heads-up. It opens nothing and has no TP or SL.
gX = 'EMA Cross + Volume'
useXsig    = input.bool(true, 'Enable EMA cross signals', group = gX, tooltip = 'EMA+ / EMA- labels when price closes through an EMA on above-average volume. NOT a trade signal — it has its own two alerts, do not point an order webhook at them.')
showEMAs   = input.bool(true, 'Plot the fast/slow EMAs', group = gX)
emaFastLen = input.int(10, 'Fast EMA', options = [8, 9, 10, 13, 21], group = gX)
emaSlowLen = input.int(20, 'Slow EMA', options = [20, 21, 34, 50], group = gX, tooltip = 'The exact pair does not matter much — 10/20, 9/21 and 8/20 all behave similarly.')
xWhich     = input.string('Fast', 'Cross which EMA', options = ['Fast', 'Slow', 'Both'], group = gX, tooltip = 'Both = price must close through the fast EMA AND already be the right side of the slow one.')
volMult    = input.float(1.2, 'Volume must exceed avg by', minval = 1.0, step = 0.1, group = gX, tooltip = '1.2 = 120% of the volume average set in the Trend-Setting Candle group. Raise it to demand a bigger surge and get fewer signals.')
skipBars   = input.int(4, 'Skip first N bars of session', minval = 0, maxval = 24, group = gX, tooltip = '4 bars on a 5-min chart = the first 20 minutes are ignored. The strong move usually comes after the open settles.')
xInWindow  = input.bool(false, 'Only during alert window', group = gX, tooltip = 'OFF means EMA crosses fire all session. The trade engine still respects the alert window regardless.')

// ── Sweep + reclaim  [from the GD layer] ──
gSw = 'Sweep + Reclaim'
showSweeps = input.bool(true, 'Mark sweep + reclaim', group = gSw, tooltip = 'A sweep is price trading THROUGH a session level and then CLOSING back on the original side — a failed break, with whoever chased it now trapped. Diamond below the bar when a low is swept and reclaimed, above the bar when a high is. Marker only.')

getPos(string p) =>
    p == 'Top Right' ? position.top_right : p == 'Top Center' ? position.top_center : position.middle_right

// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// TIME GATES
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
inRTH   = not na(time(timeframe.period, rthSess, tzSess))
inPM    = not na(time(timeframe.period, pmSess, tzSess))
inAsia  = not na(time(timeframe.period, asiaSess, tzSess))
inAlert = not na(time(timeframe.period, alertWindow, tzSess))
beforeFlat = not na(time(timeframe.period, flatSess, tzSess))

onTF = not lockTF or (timeframe.isminutes and timeframe.multiplier == math.round(str.tonumber(signalTF)))
bgcolor(showWindowBg and inAlert ? color.new(color.blue, 95) : na, title = 'Alert Window Background')
tick = syminfo.mintick
buf  = bufTicks * tick

atr    = ta.atr(14)
volAvg = ta.sma(volume, volLen)

// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// LEVELS — marked before the open, exactly the set he lists
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
var float pmH = na
var float pmL = na
if inPM
    pmH := inPM[1] ? math.max(pmH, high) : high
    pmL := inPM[1] ? math.min(pmL, low)  : low

var float asiaH = na
var float asiaL = na
if inAsia
    asiaH := inAsia[1] ? math.max(asiaH, high) : high
    asiaL := inAsia[1] ? math.min(asiaL, low)  : low

// Today's running high/low, and yesterday's frozen at the open.
var float dayH = na
var float dayL = na
var float prevDH = na
var float prevDL = na
if inRTH
    if not inRTH[1]
        prevDH := dayH
        prevDL := dayL
        dayH := high
        dayL := low
    else
        dayH := math.max(dayH, high)
        dayL := math.min(dayL, low)

vwapVal = ta.vwap(hlc3)

// Session point of control: price bucket with the most volume so far today.
// A running max keeps this O(1) per bar instead of rescanning the whole map.
var map<float, float> volMap = map.new<float, float>()
var float poc    = na
var float pocVol = 0.0
if inRTH and not inRTH[1]
    volMap.clear()
    poc    := na
    pocVol := 0.0
if inRTH and barstate.isconfirmed
    float bucket = pocTicks * tick
    float lvl    = math.round(close / bucket) * bucket
    float acc    = (volMap.contains(lvl) ? volMap.get(lvl) : 0.0) + volume
    volMap.put(lvl, acc)
    if acc > pocVol
        pocVol := acc
        poc    := lvl

plot(showVWAP ? vwapVal : na, 'VWAP', color.new(color.blue, 20), 1)

// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// OPENING RANGE — the first N minutes, then locked
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
var float orbH    = na
var float orbL    = na
var int   orbStart = na
var int   sessOpen = na
var bool  orbLocked = false
var line  orbHLine = na
var line  orbLLine = na

newSession = inRTH and not inRTH[1]
orbBuilding = inRTH and not na(sessOpen) and (time - sessOpen) < orbMins * 60000

if newSession
    sessOpen  := time
    orbStart  := bar_index
    orbH      := high
    orbL      := low
    orbLocked := false
else if orbBuilding
    orbH := math.max(orbH, high)
    orbL := math.min(orbL, low)
else if inRTH and not orbLocked and not na(orbH)
    orbLocked := true      // range is set; hunting begins

orbMid = na(orbH) or na(orbL) ? na : (orbH + orbL) / 2.0

// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// LEFT ANCHOR FOR EVERY LEVEL LINE
// The bar index of each session open is remembered in a small rolling list. The
// level lines below start at the open of the session `extendDays` back — 1 means
// yesterday's open — and run right to the live candle. Older entries are dropped
// so the list never grows past what the input can reach.
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
var int[] sessStarts = array.new_int()
if newSession
    array.push(sessStarts, bar_index)
    if array.size(sessStarts) > 12
        array.shift(sessStarts)

// Declared from bar_index so the type is series int from the outset, and so the
// fallback is already in place before any session open has been seen. The index is
// clamped, which makes a chart holding fewer sessions than asked for fall back to
// the oldest one on record instead of erroring.
int lvlX1 = math.max(0, bar_index - 20)
if array.size(sessStarts) > 0
    lvlX1 := array.get(sessStarts, math.max(0, array.size(sessStarts) - 1 - extendDays))

// The range lines start at the same left anchor as every other level, so the ORB
// high and low reach back over the previous session too.
if showORB and barstate.islast and not na(orbH)
    line.delete(orbHLine)
    line.delete(orbLLine)
    int orbX1 = math.min(orbStart, lvlX1)
    orbHLine := line.new(orbX1, orbH, bar_index, orbH, color = orbHiCol, width = 2)
    orbLLine := line.new(orbX1, orbL, bar_index, orbL, color = orbLoCol, width = 2)

// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// SETUP STATE — the armed entry zone left behind by the trend-setting candle
// Declared up here because the break tests below read setDir.
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
var int   setDir   = 0    // +1 armed long, -1 armed short, 0 none
var float tcHi     = na   // trend-setting candle extremes (also the stop)
var float tcLo     = na
var float zoneHi   = na   // entry zone bounds
var float zoneLo   = na
var int   setBar   = na
var bool  twoBarOn = false

// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// TREND-SETTING CANDLE
// A 5-minute CLOSE beyond the range that also passes his quality tests.
// Fail any test and there is no setup — the script keeps waiting.
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
candleRng = high - low
bodyOK    = candleRng > 0 and (math.abs(close - open) / candleRng) >= minBodyPct / 100.0
volOK     = not needVolUp or (volume > volAvg and volume > volume[1])
isAnomaly = useAnomaly and candleRng > atr * anomalyMlt and volume < volAvg
qualityOK = bodyOK and volOK and not isAnomaly

// ONE setup per excursion beyond the range.
// Without this guard the script re-armed on EVERY bar that stayed beyond the level,
// which pushed setBar forward each time — and since the entry requires
// bar_index > setBar, the pullback test could never pass. No entry would ever fire in
// a sustained trend, which is exactly the "only one signal in the whole backtest"
// symptom. armedRun clears when price closes back inside the range, so a genuine
// second break later in the day can still arm a fresh setup.
var bool armedRun = false
backInside = not na(orbH) and close <= orbH and close >= orbL
if backInside or newSession
    armedRun := false

brokeUp = orbLocked and inRTH and close > orbH and qualityOK and not armedRun and setDir == 0
brokeDn = orbLocked and inRTH and close < orbL and qualityOK and not armedRun and setDir == 0

// Arm a fresh setup on a valid break.
if barstate.isconfirmed and (brokeUp or brokeDn)
    setDir   := brokeUp ? 1 : -1
    tcHi     := high
    tcLo     := low
    setBar   := bar_index
    twoBarOn := false
    armedRun := true      // no further arming until price returns inside the range
    float r  = high - low
    if brokeUp
        zoneHi := high - 0.5   * r     // shallower edge of the golden pocket
        zoneLo := high - 0.618 * r     // deeper edge
    else
        zoneLo := low + 0.5   * r
        zoneHi := low + 0.618 * r

// TWO-BAR SETUP: the move extended with a second aggressive candle in the same
// direction on rising volume. He uses this when price never comes back to 0.5, so
// the zone is re-measured across BOTH candles and made shallower.
if useTwoBar and barstate.isconfirmed and setDir != 0 and bar_index == setBar + 1 and qualityOK
    bool extendUp = setDir ==  1 and close > close[1] and high > tcHi
    bool extendDn = setDir == -1 and close < close[1] and low  < tcLo
    if extendUp or extendDn
        tcHi     := math.max(tcHi, high)
        tcLo     := math.min(tcLo, low)
        setBar   := bar_index
        twoBarOn := true
        float r2 = tcHi - tcLo
        if setDir == 1
            zoneHi := tcHi - twoBarLo * r2
            zoneLo := tcHi - twoBarHi * r2
        else
            zoneLo := tcLo + twoBarLo * r2
            zoneHi := tcLo + twoBarHi * r2

// Expire a stale setup, or one invalidated by price closing back inside the range.
if barstate.isconfirmed and setDir != 0
    bool expired   = bar_index - setBar > validBars
    bool invalid   = setDir == 1 ? close < orbL : close > orbH
    if expired or invalid or not inRTH
        setDir := 0
        zoneHi := na
        zoneLo := na

// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// STACKED KEY LEVEL — his highest-probability condition
// True when price is sitting on one of the marked levels at the same time as the
// fib zone. Optional filter; always shown on the dashboard.
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
nearLvl(float px, float lvl) => na(lvl) ? false : math.abs(px - lvl) <= confluPts
stacked = nearLvl(close, pmH) or nearLvl(close, pmL) or nearLvl(close, prevDH) or
     nearLvl(close, prevDL) or nearLvl(close, asiaH) or nearLvl(close, asiaL) or
     nearLvl(close, vwapVal) or nearLvl(close, poc) or nearLvl(close, orbMid)

// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// FAST / SLOW EMA PAIR   [GD layer]
// Purely a visual trend read and the input to the cross signals below. Nothing in
// the trade engine consults these.
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
emaF = ta.ema(close, emaFastLen)
emaS = ta.ema(close, emaSlowLen)
plot(showEMAs ? emaF : na, 'EMA fast', color.new(color.teal, 20))
plot(showEMAs ? emaS : na, 'EMA slow', color.new(color.gray, 20))

// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// SWEEP + RECLAIM   [GD layer]
// Price traded THROUGH a session level and then CLOSED back on the original side.
// A failed break: whoever chased it is trapped. Marker only — no position, no alert.
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// below = true  -> a LOW being swept  (wick under it, close back above)
// below = false -> a HIGH being swept (wick over it, close back below)
swept(float lvl, bool below) =>
    bool r = false
    if not na(lvl)
        r := below ? (low < lvl and close > lvl) : (high > lvl and close < lvl)
    r

bullSweep = swept(pmL, true)  or swept(prevDL, true)
bearSweep = swept(pmH, false) or swept(prevDH, false)

plotshape(showSweeps and bullSweep, 'Sweep low',  shape.diamond, location.belowbar, color.new(color.aqua, 40),    size = size.tiny)
plotshape(showSweeps and bearSweep, 'Sweep high', shape.diamond, location.abovebar, color.new(color.fuchsia, 40), size = size.tiny)

// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// EMA CROSS ON VOLUME   [GD layer]
// EMA+ below the bar: price CLOSED up through the fast EMA on above-average volume.
// EMA- above the bar: the same downward.
// All four must hold: a genuine cross this bar, volume above its average x the
// multiplier, at least N bars past the open, and inside the session on the right
// timeframe. A cross on a thin drift gets no label.
//
// THIS IS NOT A TRADE. It has its own two alerts and no TP or SL.
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
strongVol = volume > volAvg * volMult

// Bars since the session opened, so the noisy first N can be skipped.
var int rthBarCount = 0
if newSession
    rthBarCount := 0
else if inRTH
    rthBarCount += 1
pastOpen = rthBarCount >= skipBars

xUpFast = ta.crossover(close, emaF)
xDnFast = ta.crossunder(close, emaF)
xUpSlow = ta.crossover(close, emaS)
xDnSlow = ta.crossunder(close, emaS)

// 'Both' is the strictest: cross the fast EMA AND already be the right side of the slow.
xUpRaw = xWhich == 'Fast' ? xUpFast : xWhich == 'Slow' ? xUpSlow : (xUpFast and close > emaS)
xDnRaw = xWhich == 'Fast' ? xDnFast : xWhich == 'Slow' ? xDnSlow : (xDnFast and close < emaS)

xBuy  = useXsig and barstate.isconfirmed and xUpRaw and strongVol and pastOpen and
     inRTH and (not xInWindow or inAlert) and onTF
xSell = useXsig and barstate.isconfirmed and xDnRaw and strongVol and pastOpen and
     inRTH and (not xInWindow or inAlert) and onTF

plotshape(xBuy,  'EMA Cross Buy',  shape.labelup,   location.belowbar, color.new(color.lime, 20),   text = 'EMA+', textcolor = color.black, size = size.tiny)
plotshape(xSell, 'EMA Cross Sell', shape.labeldown, location.abovebar, color.new(color.orange, 20), text = 'EMA-', textcolor = color.black, size = size.tiny)

// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// POSITION STATE
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
var int   pos     = 0
var float entryPx = na
var float slPx    = na
var float tp1Px   = na
var float tp2Px   = na
var float tp3Px   = na
var float riskPts = na
var bool  tp1Done = false
var bool  tp2Done = false
var bool  tp3Done = false
var int   entryBar = na
var int   tradesToday = 0
var int   lossesToday = 0

if newSession
    tradesToday := 0
    lossesToday := 0

// His two hard limits, plus the clock.
canTrade = tradesToday < maxTrades and lossesToday < maxLosses and inAlert and onTF and pos == 0

// ── Has price reached the entry zone? ──
// bar_index > setBar is essential: the zone is measured INSIDE the trend-setting
// candle, so without this the entry would trigger on that candle itself instead of
// waiting for the pullback he actually trades.
pullback = setDir != 0 and bar_index > setBar
inZone  = pullback and not na(zoneLo) and low <= zoneHi and high >= zoneLo
// The simpler first-webinar entry: a touch of the broken level itself.
atLevel = not pullback ? false : setDir == 1 ? (low <= orbH and close > orbH) : (high >= orbL and close < orbL)

trigger = entryMode == 'Golden Pocket' ? inZone : entryMode == 'Level Retest' ? atLevel : (inZone or atLevel)

// ── WHICH TRIGGERS CAN FIRE MID-CANDLE ──
// inZone is built from the bar's RUNNING high and low. Those only ever widen as the
// candle forms, so once the zone is touched inZone is true and STAYS true through the
// close. Firing it early therefore cannot repaint: the bar-close result is identical,
// the alert simply arrives sooner. That is what makes a real-time entry safe here.
//
// atLevel is different. It tests `close > orbH`, and the close moves on every tick, so
// it can be true mid-candle and false by the end. Firing that early WOULD repaint —
// an alert would go out for a trade the script then discards. So Level Retest keeps
// waiting for the confirmed close no matter how this input is set. Golden Pocket and
// the two-bar fallback are the modes that go real time.
touchTrig = inZone
canFireEarly = rtEntry and entryMode != 'Level Retest' and touchTrig

// ── Candidate stop and risk, measured before committing ──
candSL  = setDir == 1 ? tcLo - stopPad * tick : tcHi + stopPad * tick
candRsk = setDir == 1 ? close - candSL : candSL - close
riskOK  = candRsk > 0 and (maxStopPts == 0 or candRsk <= maxStopPts)
confOK  = not useConflu or stacked

// The ARMING of a setup still requires a confirmed close beyond the range — that part
// is his non-negotiable and is untouched. What changes here is only the pullback
// entry, which fires on touch when Real-Time Entry is on.
armedFire = canFireEarly or (barstate.isconfirmed and trigger)
fireLong  = setDir ==  1 and armedFire and riskOK and confOK and canTrade
fireShort = setDir == -1 and armedFire and riskOK and confOK and canTrade

// ── Backtest log ──
var array<float> logR  = array.new_float()
var array<int>   logTP = array.new_int()
var int totalSignals = 0

if fireLong or fireShort
    entryPx := close
    slPx    := candSL
    riskPts := candRsk
    pos      := fireLong ? 1 : -1
    entryBar := bar_index
    tp1Done  := false
    tp2Done  := false
    tp3Done  := false
    float dir = fireLong ? 1.0 : -1.0
    tp1Px := entryPx + dir * tp1R * riskPts
    tp3Px := entryPx + dir * tp3R * riskPts
    // TP2 can target a new high/low of day instead of a fixed multiple, but never
    // closer than 1R — a HOD that is already behind price is not a target.
    float rTgt = entryPx + dir * tp2R * riskPts
    if tp2HodLod
        float hod = fireLong ? nz(dayH, rTgt) : nz(dayL, rTgt)
        tp2Px := fireLong ? math.max(hod, entryPx + riskPts) : math.min(hod, entryPx - riskPts)
    else
        tp2Px := rTgt
    tradesToday  += 1
    totalSignals += 1
    setDir := 0          // one setup, one trade
    zoneHi := na
    zoneLo := na

// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// REAL-TIME TP / SL — fires the moment price touches, not at bar close
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
tp1Hit = false
tp2Hit = false
tp3Hit = false
slHit  = false

// On any bar after the entry, the full high/low is the right thing to test.
//
// ON THE ENTRY BAR ITSELF the high and low cover ground price crossed BEFORE the fill,
// so testing them would score moves the trade never had. The script used to sit the
// entry bar out entirely for that reason. With a real-time entry that leaves a hole: a
// target reached seconds after the fill would not be reported until the next candle.
// So the entry bar tests `close` instead — which in real time IS the live price, tick
// by tick, and on a historical bar equals the entry price, making it inert. Either way
// nothing that happened before the fill can be credited.
live = pos != 0 and not na(entryBar)
onEntryBar = live and bar_index == entryBar
hiTest = onEntryBar ? close : high
loTest = onEntryBar ? close : low

if live and pos == 1
    if not tp1Done and hiTest >= tp1Px - buf
        tp1Hit  := true
        tp1Done := true
        if beAfterTP1
            slPx := entryPx
    if tp1Done and not tp2Done and hiTest >= tp2Px - buf
        tp2Hit  := true
        tp2Done := true
    if tp2Done and not tp3Done and hiTest >= tp3Px - buf
        tp3Hit  := true
        tp3Done := true
    if not tp3Done and loTest <= slPx + buf
        slHit := true

if live and pos == -1
    if not tp1Done and loTest <= tp1Px + buf
        tp1Hit  := true
        tp1Done := true
        if beAfterTP1
            slPx := entryPx
    if tp1Done and not tp2Done and loTest <= tp2Px + buf
        tp2Hit  := true
        tp2Done := true
    if tp2Done and not tp3Done and loTest <= tp3Px + buf
        tp3Hit  := true
        tp3Done := true
    if not tp3Done and hiTest >= slPx - buf
        slHit := true

// ── Close the trade and log it, position-weighted ──
// A trade that trimmed at TP1 and then stopped at break-even is NOT a zero — the
// trimmed portion was banked. Scoring it as 0R would understate results badly.
if barstate.isconfirmed and pos != 0 and (slHit or tp3Done)
    float realised = 0.0
    if not tp1Done
        realised := -1.0                                  // stopped before any trim
    else
        realised := trimPct * tp1R                        // banked at TP1
        float remain = 1.0 - trimPct
        if tp3Done
            realised += (remain * 0.5) * tp2R + (remain * 0.5) * tp3R
        else if tp2Done
            realised += remain * tp2R
        // else the runner came back to break-even and adds nothing
    array.push(logR, realised)
    array.push(logTP, tp3Done ? 3 : tp2Done ? 2 : tp1Done ? 1 : 0)
    if not tp1Done
        lossesToday += 1                                  // counts against the circuit breaker
    pos     := 0
    entryPx := na
    slPx    := na
    tp1Px   := na
    tp2Px   := na
    tp3Px   := na

// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// FLATTEN — nothing may be left open past the deadline
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
var bool flatSent = false
if beforeFlat
    flatSent := false

closeAll = false
if not flatSent and onTF and pos != 0 and (not beforeFlat or not inRTH)
    closeAll := true
    flatSent := true
    if barstate.isconfirmed
        array.push(logR, tp1Done ? trimPct * tp1R : 0.0)
        array.push(logTP, tp1Done ? 1 : 0)
        pos     := 0
        entryPx := na
        slPx    := na
        tp1Px   := na
        tp2Px   := na
        tp3Px   := na

// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// HIDDEN PLOTS — reference these in the alert message as {{plot("SL")}} etc.
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
var float pSL  = na
var float pTP1 = na
var float pTP2 = na
var float pTP3 = na
var float pENT = na
if not na(slPx)
    pSL := slPx
if not na(tp1Px)
    pTP1 := tp1Px
if not na(tp2Px)
    pTP2 := tp2Px
if not na(tp3Px)
    pTP3 := tp3Px
if not na(entryPx)
    pENT := entryPx
plot(pSL,  'SL',    display = display.data_window, color = color.new(color.red, 100))
plot(pTP1, 'TP 1',  display = display.data_window, color = color.new(color.green, 100))
plot(pTP2, 'TP 2',  display = display.data_window, color = color.new(color.green, 100))
plot(pTP3, 'TP 3',  display = display.data_window, color = color.new(color.green, 100))
plot(pENT, 'Entry', display = display.data_window, color = color.new(color.blue, 100))

// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// ALERTS — names match the previous script so existing webhooks carry over
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
alertcondition(fireLong or fireShort, 'Buy / Sell')
alertcondition(fireLong,  'Buy')
alertcondition(fireShort, 'Sell')
alertcondition(tp1Hit and onTF, 'Take Profit 1')
alertcondition(tp2Hit and onTF, 'Take Profit 2')
alertcondition(tp3Hit and onTF, 'Take Profit 3')
alertcondition(slHit  and onTF, 'Stop Loss')
alertcondition(closeAll, 'Close All / Flatten')
// The last two are the GD heads-up, NOT trade signals. They open nothing and have
// no TP or SL — do not point an order webhook at them unless you mean to.
alertcondition(xBuy,  'EMA Cross Buy (volume)')
alertcondition(xSell, 'EMA Cross Sell (volume)')

// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// CHART MARKERS
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
plotshape(fireLong,  'Entry Buy',  shape.labelup,   location.belowbar, color.new(color.green, 0), text = 'BUY',  textcolor = color.white, size = size.small)
plotshape(fireShort, 'Entry Sell', shape.labeldown, location.abovebar, color.new(color.red, 0),   text = 'SELL', textcolor = color.white, size = size.small)
// plotshape needs a CONST location, so each exit gets one shape per direction —
// marks sit on the side price came from.
plotshape(tp1Hit and pos ==  1, 'TP1 L', shape.xcross, location.abovebar, color.new(color.green, 0), text = 'TP 1', textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny)
plotshape(tp1Hit and pos == -1, 'TP1 S', shape.xcross, location.belowbar, color.new(color.green, 0), text = 'TP 1', textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny)
plotshape(tp2Hit and pos ==  1, 'TP2 L', shape.xcross, location.abovebar, color.new(color.green, 0), text = 'TP 2', textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny)
plotshape(tp2Hit and pos == -1, 'TP2 S', shape.xcross, location.belowbar, color.new(color.green, 0), text = 'TP 2', textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny)
plotshape(tp3Hit and pos ==  1, 'TP3 L', shape.xcross, location.abovebar, color.new(color.lime, 0),  text = 'TP 3', textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny)
plotshape(tp3Hit and pos == -1, 'TP3 S', shape.xcross, location.belowbar, color.new(color.lime, 0),  text = 'TP 3', textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny)
plotshape(slHit  and pos ==  1, 'SL L',  shape.xcross, location.belowbar, color.new(color.red, 0),   text = 'SL',   textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny)
plotshape(slHit  and pos == -1, 'SL S',  shape.xcross, location.abovebar, color.new(color.red, 0),   text = 'SL',   textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny)
plotshape(closeAll, 'Close All', shape.xcross, location.abovebar, color.new(color.orange, 0), text = 'CLOSE', textcolor = color.white, size = size.tiny)

// The armed entry zone (the yellow pair): the 0.5 and 0.618 fib of the trend-setting
// candle. Visible only while a setup is armed — it disappears the moment the entry
// fires or the setup expires.
zoneLive = showZone and setDir != 0 and not na(zoneLo)
plot(zoneLive ? zoneHi : na, 'Golden pocket 0.5',   color.new(color.yellow, 30), 1, plot.style_linebr)
plot(zoneLive ? zoneLo : na, 'Golden pocket 0.618', color.new(color.yellow, 30), 1, plot.style_linebr)

// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// TRADE LEVEL LINES — drawn for EVERY trade, not just the live one
// On each entry, five horizontal lines are created at Entry / SL / TP1 / TP2 / TP3.
// They extend rightward for the rest of that trading day and then freeze, so past
// trades keep their levels on the chart and you can see exactly where each target
// sat — including targets price never reached.
// Old sets are not deleted; Pine drops the oldest once max_lines_count is reached,
// which keeps roughly the last hundred trades visible.
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
var line lnEnt = na
var line lnSl  = na
var line lnT1  = na
var line lnT2  = na
var line lnT3  = na
var bool linesLive = false

if showTradeLines and (fireLong or fireShort)
    lnEnt := line.new(bar_index, entryPx, bar_index, entryPx, color = color.new(color.blue, 20),  width = 1)
    lnSl  := line.new(bar_index, slPx,    bar_index, slPx,    color = color.new(color.red, 20),   width = 1, style = line.style_dashed)
    lnT1  := line.new(bar_index, tp1Px,   bar_index, tp1Px,   color = color.new(color.green, 20), width = 1, style = line.style_dashed)
    lnT2  := line.new(bar_index, tp2Px,   bar_index, tp2Px,   color = color.new(color.green, 40), width = 1, style = line.style_dashed)
    lnT3  := line.new(bar_index, tp3Px,   bar_index, tp3Px,   color = color.new(color.lime, 40),  width = 1, style = line.style_dashed)
    linesLive := true

// Stretch the current set to the live candle, then stop at the session boundary.
if linesLive
    if inRTH
        line.set_x2(lnEnt, bar_index)
        line.set_x2(lnSl,  bar_index)
        line.set_x2(lnT1,  bar_index)
        line.set_x2(lnT2,  bar_index)
        line.set_x2(lnT3,  bar_index)
    else
        linesLive := false      // day is over; freeze this set where it is

// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// LEVEL LINES AND LABELS
// Each level is a full line running from the left anchor (the open of the session
// `extendDays` back — yesterday's open by default) to the live candle, with its
// name and price at the right-hand end so nothing needs scrolling to be read.
// Everything here is rebuilt from scratch on the final bar, so nothing accumulates.
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
var line[]  lvlL = array.new_line()
var label[] lvlT = array.new_label()

drawLvl(float px, string txt, color c, int wid) =>
    if not na(px)
        array.push(lvlL, line.new(lvlX1, px, bar_index, px, color = c, width = wid))
        if showLbls
            array.push(lvlT, label.new(bar_index, px, txt + '  ' + str.tostring(px, format.mintick), color = color.new(c, 100), textcolor = c, style = label.style_label_left, size = size.small))

if barstate.islast
    for l in lvlL
        line.delete(l)
    lvlL.clear()
    for t in lvlT
        label.delete(t)
    lvlT.clear()
    if showPM
        drawLvl(pmH, 'PM High', color.orange, 2)
        drawLvl(pmL, 'PM Low',  color.orange, 2)
    if showPrevD
        drawLvl(prevDH, 'Prev Day High', #5b9cf6, 2)
        drawLvl(prevDL, 'Prev Day Low',  #5b9cf6, 2)
    if showAsia
        drawLvl(asiaH, 'Asia High', color.purple, 1)
        drawLvl(asiaL, 'Asia Low',  color.purple, 1)
    if showPOC
        drawLvl(poc, 'POC', color.red, 1)
    if showMid
        drawLvl(orbMid, 'ORB Mid', color.gray, 1)
    // VWAP is a moving line so it stays plotted; it only needs the label.
    if showVWAP and showLbls and not na(vwapVal)
        array.push(lvlT, label.new(bar_index, vwapVal, 'VWAP  ' + str.tostring(vwapVal, format.mintick), color = color.new(color.blue, 100), textcolor = color.blue, style = label.style_label_left, size = size.small))
    // The ORB high/low lines are drawn up in the opening-range section, from the same
    // left anchor as everything here; they only need naming.
    if showORB and showLbls and not na(orbH)
        array.push(lvlT, label.new(bar_index, orbH, 'ORB High  ' + str.tostring(orbH, format.mintick), color = color.new(orbHiCol, 100), textcolor = orbHiCol, style = label.style_label_left, size = size.small))
        array.push(lvlT, label.new(bar_index, orbL, 'ORB Low  '  + str.tostring(orbL, format.mintick), color = color.new(orbLoCol, 100), textcolor = orbLoCol, style = label.style_label_left, size = size.small))
    // Live trade levels, named with the R multiple each one represents.
    if showTradeLbls and pos != 0
        array.push(lvlT, label.new(bar_index, tp3Px, 'TP3 (' + str.tostring(tp3R, '#.##') + 'R)  ' + str.tostring(tp3Px, format.mintick), color = color.new(color.lime, 100),  textcolor = color.lime,  style = label.style_label_left, size = size.small))
        array.push(lvlT, label.new(bar_index, tp2Px, 'TP2 (' + str.tostring(tp2R, '#.##') + 'R)  ' + str.tostring(tp2Px, format.mintick), color = color.new(color.green, 100), textcolor = color.green, style = label.style_label_left, size = size.small))
        array.push(lvlT, label.new(bar_index, tp1Px, 'TP1 (' + str.tostring(tp1R, '#.##') + 'R)  ' + str.tostring(tp1Px, format.mintick), color = color.new(color.green, 100), textcolor = color.green, style = label.style_label_left, size = size.small))
        array.push(lvlT, label.new(bar_index, slPx,  'SL  ' + str.tostring(slPx, format.mintick), color = color.new(color.red, 100), textcolor = color.red, style = label.style_label_left, size = size.small))

// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// DASHBOARD
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
bg = #3b3b3b43
if barstate.islast and showDash
    var table d = table.new(getPos(dashPos), 2, 10, bgcolor = bg, frame_width = 2, frame_color = color.black, border_width = 1, border_color = color.black)
    string st = pos == 1 ? 'LONG' : pos == -1 ? 'SHORT' : setDir == 1 ? 'ARMED LONG' : setDir == -1 ? 'ARMED SHORT' : orbLocked ? 'WAITING' : 'RANGE FORMING'
    color  sc = pos == 1 ? color.green : pos == -1 ? color.red : setDir != 0 ? color.orange : bg
    table.merge_cells(d, 0, 0, 1, 0)
    table.cell(d, 0, 0, 'JDUN | 15m ORB', text_color = color.white, bgcolor = bg)
    table.cell(d, 0, 1, 'State', text_color = color.white, bgcolor = bg)
    table.cell(d, 1, 1, st, text_color = color.white, bgcolor = sc)
    table.cell(d, 0, 2, 'Trades / Losses', text_color = color.white, bgcolor = bg)
    table.cell(d, 1, 2, str.tostring(tradesToday) + '/' + str.tostring(maxTrades) + '   ' + str.tostring(lossesToday) + '/' + str.tostring(maxLosses), text_color = tradesToday >= maxTrades or lossesToday >= maxLosses ? color.orange : color.white, bgcolor = bg)
    table.cell(d, 0, 3, 'Setup', text_color = color.white, bgcolor = bg)
    table.cell(d, 1, 3, setDir == 0 ? '—' : (twoBarOn ? 'Two-bar' : 'Golden pocket'), text_color = color.white, bgcolor = bg)
    table.cell(d, 0, 4, 'Entry zone', text_color = color.white, bgcolor = bg)
    table.cell(d, 1, 4, setDir == 0 ? '—' : str.tostring(zoneLo, format.mintick) + ' - ' + str.tostring(zoneHi, format.mintick), text_color = color.white, bgcolor = bg)
    table.cell(d, 0, 5, 'Stacked level', text_color = color.white, bgcolor = bg)
    table.cell(d, 1, 5, stacked ? 'YES' : 'no', text_color = stacked ? color.lime : color.silver, bgcolor = bg)
    table.cell(d, 0, 6, 'Risk if taken', text_color = color.white, bgcolor = bg)
    table.cell(d, 1, 6, setDir == 0 ? '—' : str.tostring(candRsk, '#.##') + ' pts' + (riskOK ? '' : '  TOO WIDE'), text_color = setDir == 0 ? color.white : riskOK ? color.white : color.red, bgcolor = bg)
    table.cell(d, 0, 7, 'Entry / SL', text_color = color.white, bgcolor = bg)
    table.cell(d, 1, 7, pos == 0 ? '—' : str.tostring(entryPx, format.mintick) + ' / ' + str.tostring(slPx, format.mintick), text_color = color.white, bgcolor = bg)
    table.cell(d, 0, 8, 'Signal TF', text_color = color.white, bgcolor = bg)
    table.cell(d, 1, 8, onTF ? 'OK' : 'WRONG TF', text_color = onTF ? color.lime : color.red, bgcolor = bg)
    // Context only — the EMA pair gates nothing in the trade engine.
    table.cell(d, 0, 9, 'EMA trend', text_color = color.white, bgcolor = bg)
    table.cell(d, 1, 9, emaF > emaS ? 'UP' : emaF < emaS ? 'DOWN' : 'flat', text_color = emaF > emaS ? color.lime : emaF < emaS ? color.red : color.silver, bgcolor = bg)

// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// BACKTEST TABLE — everything in R, since that is how he sizes
// A bar-close simulation. If a TP and the SL are both touched inside one candle
// this credits the TP, because intrabar order is not knowable.
// ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
if barstate.islast and showBT
    var table b = table.new(getPos(btPos), 2, 11, bgcolor = bg, frame_width = 2, frame_color = color.black, border_width = 1, border_color = color.black)
    int n = array.size(logR)
    int wins = 0
    int losses = 0
    int h1 = 0
    int h2 = 0
    int h3 = 0
    float sumR = 0.0
    float grossW = 0.0
    float grossL = 0.0
    if n > 0
        for i = 0 to n - 1
            float r = array.get(logR, i)
            int tpn = array.get(logTP, i)
            sumR += r
            if r > 0
                wins += 1
                grossW += r
            else if r < 0
                losses += 1
                grossL += math.abs(r)
            if tpn >= 1
                h1 += 1
            if tpn >= 2
                h2 += 1
            if tpn >= 3
                h3 += 1
    float pf   = grossL > 0 ? grossW / grossL : na
    float wr   = (wins + losses) > 0 ? 100.0 * wins / (wins + losses) : na
    float avgR = n > 0 ? sumR / n : na

    table.merge_cells(b, 0, 0, 1, 0)
    table.cell(b, 0, 0, 'Backtest (R)', text_color = color.white, bgcolor = bg)
    table.cell(b, 0, 1, 'Signals', text_color = color.white, bgcolor = bg)
    table.cell(b, 1, 1, str.tostring(totalSignals), text_color = color.white, bgcolor = bg)
    table.cell(b, 0, 2, 'Closed', text_color = color.white, bgcolor = bg)
    table.cell(b, 1, 2, str.tostring(n), text_color = color.white, bgcolor = bg)
    table.cell(b, 0, 3, 'Wins', text_color = color.white, bgcolor = bg)
    table.cell(b, 1, 3, str.tostring(wins), text_color = color.lime, bgcolor = bg)
    table.cell(b, 0, 4, 'Losses', text_color = color.white, bgcolor = bg)
    table.cell(b, 1, 4, str.tostring(losses), text_color = color.red, bgcolor = bg)
    table.cell(b, 0, 5, 'Win rate', text_color = color.white, bgcolor = bg)
    table.cell(b, 1, 5, na(wr) ? '—' : str.tostring(wr, '#.#') + '%', text_color = color.white, bgcolor = bg)
    table.cell(b, 0, 6, 'Profit factor', text_color = color.white, bgcolor = bg)
    table.cell(b, 1, 6, na(pf) ? '—' : str.tostring(pf, '#.##'), text_color = na(pf) ? color.white : pf >= 1.5 ? color.lime : pf >= 1.0 ? color.yellow : color.red, bgcolor = bg)
    table.cell(b, 0, 7, 'Total R', text_color = color.white, bgcolor = bg)
    table.cell(b, 1, 7, str.tostring(sumR, '#.##') + 'R', text_color = sumR >= 0 ? color.lime : color.red, bgcolor = bg)
    table.cell(b, 0, 8, 'Avg R / trade', text_color = color.white, bgcolor = bg)
    table.cell(b, 1, 8, na(avgR) ? '—' : str.tostring(avgR, '#.##') + 'R', text_color = color.white, bgcolor = bg)
    table.merge_cells(b, 0, 9, 1, 9)
    table.cell(b, 0, 9, '── TP hits ──', text_color = color.white, bgcolor = bg)
    table.cell(b, 0, 10, 'TP1 / TP2 / TP3', text_color = color.white, bgcolor = bg)
    table.cell(b, 1, 10, str.tostring(h1) + ' / ' + str.tostring(h2) + ' / ' + str.tostring(h3), text_color = color.white, bgcolor = bg)
